        "extraction_profile": "pypdf-6.14.2-whitespace-normalized.v0.1",
        "normalized_text_window": "USA V. HOLMES 9 After a two -and-a-half-year investigation, a grand jury returned an indictment against Holmes and Balwani. They were tried separately in lengthy jury trials, and each was convicted on numerous fraud charges. Holmes and Balwani now bring several challenges to the district court’s decisions at trial and sentencing. We affirm. Factual Background The Third Superseding Indictment (the “Indictment”) charged Holmes and Balwani (co",
        "normalized_text_window_sha256": "sha256:8555ab3668e36cf3287c2b84dec16919f32b53b80e18f07c12363b13d652475e",
        "page_number": 9,
        "required_fragment": "We affirm.",
        "source_ref": "source:theranos:ca9:22-10312-amended"
      },
      {
        "anchor_ref": "anchor:theranos:ca9:holmes-investor-counts",
        "extraction_profile": "pypdf-6.14.2-whitespace-normalized.v0.1",
        "normalized_text_window": "ly four months. A. Holmes’s Conviction and Sentence During Holmes’s trial, the government dismissed Count 9. The jury acquitted Holmes on the patient -related counts: conspiracy (Count 2) and wire fraud (Counts 10 –12). The jury convicted Holmes of four investor -related counts: the investor-related conspi racy (Count 1), and wire fraud relating to three investor -victims (Counts 6 –8). The jury hung on the wire -fraud counts related to C -1 investors (Counts 3–5). At Holmes’s sentencing, the d",
        "normalized_text_window_sha256": "sha256:f804a3502838fbca205444261a52cbc51cc702ff8f8feca7603cea1630c7e633",
        "page_number": 16,
        "required_fragment": "The jury convicted Holmes of four investor -related counts:",
        "source_ref": "source:theranos:ca9:22-10312-amended"
      },
      {
        "anchor_ref": "anchor:theranos:ca9:holmes-patient-acquittal",
        "extraction_profile": "pypdf-6.14.2-whitespace-normalized.v0.1",
        "normalized_text_window": "relationship. Holmes was tried first in late 2021. Balwani was then tried in early 2022. Each trial lasted nearly four months. A. Holmes’s Conviction and Sentence During Holmes’s trial, the government dismissed Count 9. The jury acquitted Holmes on the patient -related counts: conspiracy (Count 2) and wire fraud (Counts 10 –12). The jury convicted Holmes of four investor -related counts: the investor-related conspi racy (Count 1), and wire fraud relating to three investor -victims (Counts 6 –8). The jury hung on ",
        "normalized_text_window_sha256": "sha256:53cc26bccc61a19e1d1bf7d603fbe794c009b69f1b924bc6e9ab8c78c36ba5d8",
        "page_number": 16,
        "required_fragment": "The jury acquitted Holmes on the patient -related counts: conspiracy (Count 2)",
        "source_ref": "source:theranos:ca9:22-10312-amended"
      }
    ],
